0-bf74-24c4f1676102" :question/math-academy-id "q-275275" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨6,-2,0⟩$ and $v=⟨5,0,-3⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$\n\n$u\\times v=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-3)-0\\cdot 0)i-(6\\cdot (-3)-0\\cdot 5)j+(6\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =(6-0)i-(-18-0)j+(0-(-10))k \\\\  & =6i+18j+10k \\\\  & =⟨6,18,10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275275/field-1" "q-275275/field-2" "q-275275/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275275"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
